Reading: gate source_commit (L977), fix_revision (L743-757), head_commit_at_start (L397-402; vhead L754 is the verifying run head_commit_at_start), review_rounds[].source_commit (L750-753, L774, L785). Candidate-manifest source_commit (L929) must equal the round (L774) or gate (L967) source_commit, so it is covered transitively. The review record's own source_commit field is only schema-validated and not used by any gate check, so it is not a field "the gate depends on". The "fourth and last" claim holds.

CONCLUSION: D-045 presents itself as delivery tooling completing D-044's commit-object class (the fourth and last field), not as a business requirement. It makes no PMI/Mobily/G1-G6/Finance/benefit claim. The census, 105-test and "fourth and last" claims are accurate. ONE INACCURACY: the heading says "(all three reviewers PASS; each raised one Low ...)", but the round-28 domain-reviewer record raised no finding (findings=[]). The same row's context column says correctly "domain PASS with no findings". Reported as Low F-DG0-015.
